Here is the translation into simple English. 

*(Note: The original text uses a lot of Hong Kong-style bilingual slang and phonetic Cantonese. I have translated the meaning and tone into natural, casual English.)*

## Alice:
Haha. 
Yeah, me too. 
I really like playing.
But I never gamble. 
:)

## Bob:
Oh... I never gamble on Big Two either ;-) 
Except for that time a few weeks ago.

## Alice:
What happened a few weeks ago?

## Bob:
I went to a friend's house.
He wanted to play Big Two.
So I said, let's play.
Then he said 1 cent per card... (because he plays very well).
So I figured, "sure, why not"... besides, at most I'd lose something like $10...

## Alice:
That's true.
:) 
Hehe. You are pretty easygoing.
It's good actually. But if I have to gamble, I wouldn't enjoy the game thoroughly.

## Bob:
But it's not very good to be too stubborn...
Yeah, if you have to gamble, it's very stressful...
By the way, do you have the program?

## Alice:
What program?
No.
Do I need to download something?
:)

## Bob:
Well, to play online, of course you need a program...
My chat client doesn't support file transfers yet... maybe you can get it from me by FTP or HTTP.... wait...

## Alice:
Okay.
:) 
Thanks a lot!
Hehe [end of text]


